        "id": "ex-two-sided-normal-z-power-includes-both-tails",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "A two-sided normal z-test retains its lower-tail power",
        "statement": "Let \\(\\alpha=0.05\\), \\(n=4\\), and \\(\\delta=\\sigma>0\\) in the known-variance normal model, with simple null \\(\\mu=\\mu_0\\) and alternative \\(\\mu=\\mu_0+\\delta\\). The two-sided test rejects for \\(|Z_n|>z_{0.975}\\). Its exact power is",
        "strategy": "direct",
        "deps": [
